exports[`git.pull.title and git.pull.description, via rhachet given: [case3] a linked repo where each refusal critipath is walked when: [t0] each refusal runs through rhachet, under --auth as-human then: each refusal is snapped from the skill first line on 1`] = `
{
  "bodyOverCap": "✋ ConstraintError: the body, with its seaturtle footer, holds 70036 characters; github caps a comment or pr description at 65536

🥥 did you know?
   └─ to fix it, pick one
      ├─ trim the body
      └─ move a section into a keyed comment: rhx git.pull.comment set --key <name> --from <file>
",
  "bodySecret": "✋ ConstraintError: the body from '@stdin' holds a secret-shaped value; a pull shows its words to every reader
   └─ shape: github token, line 3 (the value is not echoed)

🥥 did you know?
   └─ to fix it
      └─ remove the value from the body, then rerun; a credential belongs in the keyrack, never in a pull
",
  "foreignAuthor": "✋ ConstraintError: ehmpathy/surf-demo#8 was opened by reef-ranger, not by surfer-kai (as-human)
   └─ a set writes only a pull its own credential opened

🥥 did you know?
   └─ to fix it, pick one
      ├─ cat ./.temp/body.md | rhx git.pull.description.set --which 8 --from @stdin --mode plan --auth as-ehmpath   # if reef-ranger is that login: plan, then add --mode apply; pipe the same body in again
      └─ ask reef-ranger to set it; this credential may not
",
  "foreignOrg": "✋ ConstraintError: owner 'seaturtlecorp' is outside the home orgs
   └─ home org: ehmpathy

🥥 did you know?
   └─ to fix it
      └─ target a repo in one of those orgs, via --in <owner/name>
",
  "loggedOut": "✋ ConstraintError: github refused the credential (as-human) on the read of the current login
   └─ detail: To get started with GitHub CLI, please run:  gh auth login

🥥 did you know?
   └─ to fix it
      └─ gh auth login
",
  "noPull": "✋ ConstraintError: pull request ehmpathy/surf-demo#99 is absent, or surfer-kai (as-human) cannot see it

🥥 did you know?
   └─ to fix it, pick one
      ├─ check --which and --in
      ├─ drop --which to address the pull of this branch
      └─ rerun with --auth as-ehmpath
",
  "titleEmpty": "✋ ConstraintError: the title from '@stdin' is empty; a pull needs a title

🥥 did you know?
   └─ to fix it
      └─ echo 'feat(reef): map the kelp beds' | rhx git.pull.title.set --from @stdin --auth as-human --mode apply   # pipe a title that is not empty
",
  "titleMultiLine": "✋ ConstraintError: the title from '@stdin' holds a newline; a pull title is one line

🥥 did you know?
   └─ to fix it
      └─ keep the first line as the title; move the rest into the description
",
}
`;

